SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "LCC.ldr_ao16_site_cover_acreage", "instrument_version": "LCC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2015@2025-07-01", "topic": "SITE_COVER", "title": "Table 6.2.5.3.1 PO16/AO16", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SITE_COVER", "operator": "<=", "value": 20, "unit": "%", "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2025-07-01", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "LOGAN"}, {"level": "PRECINCT", "precinct": "LCC:LOW_DENSITY_RESIDENTIAL/ACREAGE"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "ldr_ao16_site_cover_acreage", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"max_site_cover\", \"operator\": \"<=\", \"value\": 20, \"unit\": \"%\", \"conditions\": [], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": null}\nStructure scope 'development (all buildings/structures)' mapped by keyword to ['ANY']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO\nResearcher notes: These precinct site cover AOs sit under the heading 'For assessable development only' (Table 6.2.5.3.1), so they are never requirements for accepted development. Not listed in Part 1 Table 1.6.1 (which lists only Dual occupancy and Dwelling house code PO3/AO3, PO4/AO4, PO5/AO5, PO6/AO6, PO7/AO7(.1), PO8/AO8, PO9/AO9, PO12/AO12 as QDC alternative provisions). Ordinary planning assessment benchmark only. Applicability caution: for a Dwelling house (and a class 10 building/structure for a Dwelling house) in a 'residential area' on Residential overlay map OM-10.00, Table 5.10.10.1 nominates only the 9.3.2 Dual occupancy and Dwelling house code as the requirement; the zone code is nominated only for class 10 buildings for residential activities other than a Dwelling house, and for other uses (e.g. MCU code assessment of other uses). Table 5.7.1 also nominates the zone code for building work for uses other than Dual occupancy (auxiliary unit)/Dwelling house. So this zone provision is generally NOT a requirement for a house or its Class 10a outbuildings. For Dwelling houses, 9.3.2 AO3 (alternative provision) gives Small lot 60%, Small acreage 35%, Acreage 20%; for Suburban/Large suburban/Village no 9.3.2 site cover -> QDC/QHC."}$q$::jsonb);
