SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "LCC.rr_ao4_boundary_clearance", "instrument_version": "LCC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2015@2025-07-01", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "Table 6.2.13.3.1 PO4/AO4", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "AO4 A building or structure, other than an existing lawful building or structure, has a minimum: a. road boundary clearance of 20 metres where it has a frontage to Mount Cotton Road or Beenleigh-Redland Bay Road or b. road boundary clearance of 10 metres on all other roads c. side and rear boundary clearance of three metres.", "extracted_value": null, "extracted_operator": "conditional"}, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2025-07-01", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "LOGAN"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "LCC:RURAL_RESIDENTIAL"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "rr_ao4_boundary_clearance", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"min_road_boundary_clearance\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"20 m to Mount Cotton Rd / Beenleigh-Redland Bay Rd\", \"10 m other roads\", \"side and rear 3 m\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": null}\nStructure scope 'A building or structure, other than an existing lawful building or structure' mapped by keyword to ['ANY']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO\nResearcher notes: Not listed in Part 1 Table 1.6.1 (which lists only Dual occupancy and Dwelling house code PO3/AO3, PO4/AO4, PO5/AO5, PO6/AO6, PO7/AO7(.1), PO8/AO8, PO9/AO9, PO12/AO12 as QDC alternative provisions). Ordinary planning assessment benchmark only. Applicability caution: for a Dwelling house (and a class 10 building/structure for a Dwelling house) in a 'residential area' on Residential overlay map OM-10.00, Table 5.10.10.1 nominates only the 9.3.2 Dual occupancy and Dwelling house code as the requirement; the zone code is nominated only for class 10 buildings for residential activities other than a Dwelling house, and for other uses (e.g. MCU code assessment of other uses). Table 5.7.1 also nominates the zone code for building work for uses other than Dual occupancy (auxiliary unit)/Dwelling house. So this zone provision is generally NOT a requirement for a house or its Class 10a outbuildings. Note: RR AO4(a) applies 20 m to any RR lot fronting these roads, whereas 9.3.2 AO4(d) applies 20 m only in the Carbrook precinct."}$q$::jsonb);
